title: 'Async Robot never calls _check_auth: missing credentials send ''Basic Og=='
updated: 2026-10-13T19:50:26Z
---

`Net::Async::Hetzner::Robot` defines `_check_auth` (`lib/Net/Async/Hetzner/Robot.pm:38`) with the helpful 'No Robot credentials configured' message, but `get`/`post`/`put`/`delete` never call it - they go straight to `$robot->_build_request`. The sync client enforces it with `around _request` (`p5-www-hetzner/lib/WWW/Hetzner/Robot.pm:135-139`), which the async path bypasses. `t/robot.t:67` only calls `_check_auth` directly.

Reproduce without HETZNER_ROBOT_USER/PASSWORD:

    my $r = Net::Async::Hetzner::Robot->new;
    $r->_robot->_build_request('GET', '/server')->headers->{Authorization}
    # Basic Og==      (= ':'), plus two 'Use of uninitialized value' warnings from WWW/Hetzner/Robot.pm line 145

The request goes out with empty credentials and comes back as a 401 from Hetzner instead of failing locally. The Cloud twin does croak, because its `token` accessor croaks.

Done when: every Robot verb checks the credentials before building the request (failed Future or croak, consistent with Cloud), with a test through `get`, not through `_check_auth`.

